WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.920
Is Loki due for another untimely&nbsp;
death? Could Spider-Man be swinging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.120
into another cinematic universe?&nbsp;
Phase 5 of the MCU is upon us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.900
but heroes beware, not everyone&nbsp;
is going to make it out alive.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:19.260
Hulk, and by extension Bruce Banner, is one of&nbsp;
the MCU's oldest characters. He first made his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:25.080
debut in the 2008 film "The Incredible Hulk" a&nbsp;
month after "Iron Man," and had a starring role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:30.600
in 2012's "The Avengers." Outside of a select&nbsp;
few superheroes, such as Thor and Hawkeye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.700
that also makes him one of the only characters who&nbsp;
has survived up until this point. With most of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.860
fellow heroes from Phase 1 of the MCU gone,&nbsp;
it could be that Hulk's story is near an end.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.780
Of course, the timing would make some sense as&nbsp;
Bruce has essentially reached a balance in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:51.300
life. Both his personalities have effectively&nbsp;
merged into one individual, giving birth to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.040
"Smart Hulk" figure we see in "Avengers: Endgame."&nbsp;
This character combines the strength of the Hulk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.480
with the intelligence of Banner and sees an&nbsp;
end to the internal struggle the hero has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.400
enduring for several years. Now that his story&nbsp;
has come full circle, it could be a good time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.680
for him to leave the MCU, especially since he has&nbsp;
helped train She-Hulk as a potential replacement.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:15.540
There's also a rights issue that looms&nbsp;
over the Hulk, stopping Disney and Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.980
Studios from being able to create a&nbsp;
standalone movie. Actor Mark Ruffalo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:24.660
explained that Universal owns the rights&nbsp;
to any film focusing entirely on the Hulk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.420
meaning Disney is limited&nbsp;
in what it can do with him.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:34.200
Vision has had a rough ride in the MCU. Created&nbsp;
by Ultron, Tony Stark, Thor, and Bruce Banner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.120
the synthezoid was brought to life with the help&nbsp;
of the Mind Stone. After battling alongside the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.620
Avengers against Ultron in Sokovia, he and&nbsp;
his fellow heroes decided to destroy the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.600
Mind Stone in an attempt to stop Thanos from&nbsp;
capturing it — a process that led to Vision's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:54.000
death at the hands of his lover Wanda Maximoff.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, Thanos reversed time and brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.700
Vision back to life only to kill him a second time&nbsp;
by forcibly removing the Mind Stone from his head.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.560
A recreation of the character was brought&nbsp;
into existence by Wanda using Chaos Magic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.180
in "WandaVision," while S.W.O.R.D. developed&nbsp;
their own version, known as White Vision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:14.580
by reassembling his parts following the Battle&nbsp;
of Wakanda. Considering how the character has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:19.920
been killed multiple times already, a more final&nbsp;
death sooner rather than later seems in the cards.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.600
"So long, darling."

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.980
At the moment, it still isn't clear what&nbsp;
the future holds for Vision. White Vision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:30.180
now believes himself to be the true version&nbsp;
of the hero, is the only remaining Vision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:34.620
and his whereabouts are unknown following&nbsp;
the events of "WandaVision." Paul Bettany&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.880
also confirmed in 2022 that he doesn't&nbsp;
have a contract with Marvel Studios,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.580
so his character's days appear numbered, although&nbsp;
a show featuring White Vision may be in the works.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.440
Although he hasn't been as important to&nbsp;
the wider MCU as some of his counterparts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.380
Hank Pym is a significant&nbsp;
player in the "Ant-Man" films.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.420
"Yes. I'm still alive"

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:58.560
He is set to appear in the third entry&nbsp;
in the series, "Ant-Man and the Wasp:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.600
Quantumania," in early 2023 in which he'll&nbsp;
explore the Quantum Realm with Scott Lang,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.460
Hope van Dyne, and Janet van Dyne. Trailers&nbsp;
have revealed that the group will encounter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:12.480
Kang the Conqueror in the Quantum Realm,&nbsp;
which might not be good news for Pym.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:18.180
After all, Kang was first introduced in "Loki"&nbsp;
in 2021 as the next big villain in the form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:23.340
of He Who Remains, a variant who dedicated his&nbsp;
life to stopping more evil variants of himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.740
from being able to take over all of existence.&nbsp;
Marvel Studios revealed Phase 6 will conclude&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:34.080
with two "Avengers" movies, with the first being&nbsp;
"Avengers: The Kang Dynasty." This suggests that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.700
Kang the Conqueror will be similar to Thanos&nbsp;
and prove to be a major villain going forward.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.080
If that's the case, there would be no better&nbsp;
way to introduce him to movie-going audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.820
as a huge threat than if he killed a major&nbsp;
character. Pym would fit the bill in that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:52.380
sense. He is already an older figure and has&nbsp;
passed on most of his knowledge to Scott,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:57.660
Hope, and Janet. His death could provide the&nbsp;
heroes of the MCU with plenty of motivation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:00.960
to take on the time-traveling&nbsp;
supervillain Kang the Conqueror.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:06.480
James Rhodes, also known as War Machine is one of&nbsp;
the most senior members of the Avengers. He made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.980
his debut in "Iron Man," where he was portrayed&nbsp;
by Terrence Howard before being replaced by Don&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:15.360
Cheadle in "Iron Man 2." While he's played a&nbsp;
somewhat significant role in the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.620
he has never had a standalone film&nbsp;
or been the main focus of a movie or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:23.340
television show. In fact, Rhodes has&nbsp;
been largely absent since "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:27.180
Endgame" except for a small role in&nbsp;
"The Falcon and The Winter Soldier."

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:33.000
A close associate of Tony Stark, War Machine will&nbsp;
take on an important role in Phase 5. Samuel L.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.920
Jackson confirmed that Cheadle would appear in&nbsp;
the upcoming Disney+ series "Secret Invasion."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.840
Meanwhile, the character has been confirmed to&nbsp;
star in the television series-turned-movie "Armor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:48.420
Wars." So James Rhodes certainly has a future in&nbsp;
the MCU. It's just unclear for how much longer.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.960
The actor has confirmed he is no&nbsp;
longer under contract with Marvel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:57.540
which might well be a hint that his future in&nbsp;
the MCU franchise is in doubt. War Machine has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:01.740
faced death before, most notably during the&nbsp;
airport battle scene in "Captain America:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:06.960
Civil War," and he may not have that many lucky&nbsp;
escapes left in him. His death would certainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:11.245
be a major event, especially following&nbsp;
the passing of his close friend Iron Man.

00:05:11.245 --> 00:05:11.280
"See you on the other side, man.”

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:17.100
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" has&nbsp;
something of a finale feel to it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:21.480
and fans have been speculating for some time&nbsp;
that it could see the deaths of several key&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:26.820
characters. Chief among them is Rocket Raccoon,&nbsp;
the cynical sentient animal that has been at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:31.620
the center of the ragtag team of mercenaries&nbsp;
throughout all of their appearances in the MCU.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:36.480
Director James Gunn spoke about the new film&nbsp;
acting as a way of wrapping up Rocket's story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.580
and exploring his origins. A trailer for the film&nbsp;
appears to show a young Rocket and features the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:45.900
hero saying that he is "done running." Combine&nbsp;
that with the fact that Gunn has previously said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:51.060
that he would explore Rocket's gruesome origin&nbsp;
story, which he described in "MCU Exchange" as:

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:54.720
"...a little bit more horrible than what it&nbsp;
is in the comics when you come down to it."

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:59.160
"Guardians of the Galaxy 3" will be Gunn's&nbsp;
last MCU project for the foreseeable future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:04.500
as he's now in charge of the DC film universe&nbsp;
for Warner Bros. All this, plus the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:09.360
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" appears to have&nbsp;
a more somber tone might mean that fans should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:14.400
get the tissues ready. At the very least, seeing&nbsp;
Rocket's full story unfold won't be easy viewing.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:18.780
Nebula is another member of the Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy who could see her time in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:23.580
the MCU come to an end during Phase 5. You&nbsp;
could argue that the adoptive daughter of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:27.240
Thanos has had one of the most redemptive&nbsp;
story arcs of any character in the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:32.160
having gone from a single-minded antagonist who&nbsp;
wanted nothing more than revenge on her stepsister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:37.140
Gamora to reconciling with Gamora and joining&nbsp;
the heroes in their fight against the Mad Titan.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:41.400
Exactly what Karen Gillan's situation is&nbsp;
in terms of her contract with Disney for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:46.200
the MCU hasn't been made public. However,&nbsp;
she has spoken about how much she enjoys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:49.440
playing the character in an interview&nbsp;
with "The Hollywood Reporter," saying

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:52.260
"I really like playing her,&nbsp;
so I'm not eager to finish."

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:56.400
However, that doesn't mean she will get to&nbsp;
continue portraying Nebula in the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.460
and Gillan has even suggested in an Instagram post&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:03.780
that "Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3"&nbsp;
could be the final outing for Nebula.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:07.380
Considering everything that has&nbsp;
gone on between Gamora and Nebula,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:11.760
it might be fitting to have one of them sacrifice&nbsp;
themselves for the other. If that were the case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:15.960
the sensible bet would be for Nebula to&nbsp;
take the fall as it would best suit her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:19.500
overall narrative as someone who has&nbsp;
changed so much over the last decade.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:25.080
Drax is another longtime member of the Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy and a familiar face in the MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:30.180
He also has one of the more tragic backstories&nbsp;
of any hero in the franchise. That's primarily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:35.640
because his beef with Thanos was far more personal&nbsp;
than many others, as Ronan the Accuser killed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:40.500
wife and daughter as part of his alliance with the&nbsp;
Mad Titan. That means that his entire motivation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:44.880
and everything he has done in the "Guardians of&nbsp;
the Galaxy" films has been tinged with sorrow.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:47.940
Despite finding a new family&nbsp;
in the Guardians of the Galaxy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.000
Drax the Destroyer clearly still&nbsp;
mourns the loss of his family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:56.040
and it seems almost certain that he will reunite&nbsp;
with them at some point. Having that happen at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.040 --> 00:08:00.900
the conclusion of "Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.&nbsp;
3" would be a fitting end for a warrior who has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:04.920
stood against some of the biggest threats the&nbsp;
universe has seen. It would also give him the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:09.960
chance to perhaps save his new family in some sort&nbsp;
of heroic act before going to his final reward.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:15.360
"And in the end, I will see&nbsp;
my wife and daughter again."

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.600
Throw in the fact that actor Dave&nbsp;
Bautista has been very clear about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:23.220
the next film being his last in the MCU, and&nbsp;
it seems almost certain that Drax will meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:26.520
his end as the character's story&nbsp;
comes to a natural conclusion.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:31.740
Thor is somewhat unique in the MCU. Not only&nbsp;
is he one of the few characters who has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:35.580
around since "The Avengers" in 2012,&nbsp;
but he has also had four solo movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.880
with the most recent being&nbsp;
"Thor: Love and Thunder." Yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:43.380
he still hasn't had a defining moment to say&nbsp;
goodbye like Captain America or Iron Man.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:47.880
That could well change in the future, with&nbsp;
Chris Hemsworth telling "Vanity Fair" that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:52.560
any future appearances in the MCU would&nbsp;
"probably be the finale" for the Norse god.

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:57.420
The ending of "Thor: Love and Thunder" provided&nbsp;
some closure to a character who has been on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:02.160
a constant search for meaning since his first&nbsp;
appearance. Now a father to his adoptive daughter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:07.200
Love, he may have found his true place in the&nbsp;
universe and be able to settle down. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:11.520
having his arc come to an end might also&nbsp;
mean he could die, causing his legacy to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:15.420
live on in those he considers part of&nbsp;
his family, including Korg and Love.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:19.500
His story will have to come to an end at&nbsp;
some point, and having him involved in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:23.400
battle with Kang the Conqueror would be&nbsp;
a perfect way to do it. The actor has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:26.640
also announced that he is taking a step&nbsp;
back from acting following his recent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:31.260
discovery that he carries an increased risk of&nbsp;
developing Alzheimer's disease later in life.

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:36.180
At the beginning of the MCU, Nick Fury&nbsp;
was a staple that helped hold all of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:41.880
various films and television series together.&nbsp;
He has been involved in 11 MCU movies and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:46.140
responsible for creating the Avengers&nbsp;
Initiative. Yet, Fury has largely been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:50.520
absent from the franchise in recent years&nbsp;
outside of brief appearances or cameos.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:55.680
All that is about to change with the release of&nbsp;
the television series "Secret Invasion" and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:59.940
movie "The Marvels," which will see Samuel&nbsp;
L. Jackson reprise the character in starring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:04.560
roles. Still, while Fury will no doubt have an&nbsp;
important part to play in those two projects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:10.140
his influence over events in Phase 5 still isn't&nbsp;
clear. And with his significance seemingly waning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:13.620
it may be time for the former Director&nbsp;
of S.H.I.E.L.D. to meet his maker.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:18.240
After all, Fury has already come close&nbsp;
to death on several occasions and could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:22.260
provide a lot of inspiration to the heroes&nbsp;
left behind — many of whom he has close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:26.100
relationships with — if he was killed.&nbsp;
It would be appropriate to have Fury&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:30.480
fall now that he has such a legacy built&nbsp;
up that will last long after his demise.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:34.620
Few people would have thought that Loki&nbsp;
would become the beloved character he has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:38.940
since his introduction. Yet, his story&nbsp;
in the MCU is a bit hard to follow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:44.100
mainly due to his complicated timeline within the&nbsp;
franchise. The character has gone from villain to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:49.020
anti-hero to a devoted ally of Thor in his fight&nbsp;
against Thanos. Yet, he has also been killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:54.120
by the Mad Titan and lives on in the form of a&nbsp;
variant who starred in the Disney+ series "Loki."

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:58.080
The God of Mischief's story is set&nbsp;
to continue in "Loki" Season 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:03.240
although it's unclear how much of a role he'll&nbsp;
play in the rest of Phase 5. Marvel Studios still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:07.260
hasn't confirmed that the character will appear&nbsp;
in any other projects. That's despite the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:11.040
that Tom Hiddleston has confirmed he would like&nbsp;
to keep playing Loki for as long as possible.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:15.360
Taking into account that Loki has already&nbsp;
been killed and will no doubt have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:19.260
confront Kang the Conqueror after he and&nbsp;
his female variant Sylvie unleashed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:23.280
villain upon the multiverse, then it&nbsp;
seems likely he could die. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:26.640
there wouldn't be anything stopping&nbsp;
other potential variants from continuing.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:32.400
Spider-Man is one of the MCU's biggest and most&nbsp;
successful heroes. He's become a significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:37.740
figure in the franchise, working alongside Iron&nbsp;
Man, Doctor Strange, and the rest of the Avengers.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:41.580
But the ending of "Spider-Man: No Way&nbsp;
Home" effectively made everyone forget&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:45.660
that Peter Parker exists. This not&nbsp;
only gave the hero the anonymity to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:50.040
operate as an independent figure outside&nbsp;
of the Avengers but also allows Sony to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:54.840
remove him from the MCU altogether. Sony and&nbsp;
Disney have had difficulty working together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.840 --> 00:12:00.197
and only struck a last-minute deal to&nbsp;
keep Holland in the MCU back in 2019.

00:12:00.197 --> 00:12:00.240
"I don't want to go, I don't want to go…"

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:08.040
It's possible that Peter's Spider-Man could depart&nbsp;
the MCU at some point, but others could follow in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:12.780
his web steps. Apart from a brief Easter egg&nbsp;
reference in "Spider-Man: Homecoming," Miles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:18.480
Morales has been entirely absent from the MCU.&nbsp;
But the latest movie did introduce the idea of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:23.160
different versions of the web-slinging hero, so&nbsp;
it's possible Miles could show up. He could even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:28.920
be a potential replacement for the MCU's Peter&nbsp;
Parker in the event that Holland's Spidey dies.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:32.940
The Winter Soldier, otherwise known as&nbsp;
Bucky Barnes, has gone through one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:37.620
biggest transformations of any character&nbsp;
within the MCU. Once a friend and ally of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:42.540
Steve Rogers, Barnes was transformed into a&nbsp;
super-soldier assassin by H.Y.D.R.A. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:46.080
he was eventually able to overcome his&nbsp;
programming with the help of Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:51.540
America and King T'Challa of Wakanda. Now a&nbsp;
hero in his own right, he has most recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:56.340
fought against the Flag Smashers alongside Sam&nbsp;
Wilson in "The Falcon and the Winter Soldier."

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:59.760
In an interview with "Uproxx,"&nbsp;
Sebastian Stan revealed that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:02.520
feels Bucky has earned himself&nbsp;
a comfortable death, stating:

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:06.600
"Hopefully at this point, it would be&nbsp;
in a nice warm bed as a 200-year-old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:09.900
man with a family. That's his way&nbsp;
now, I think he's earned that."

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:14.160
Of course, that doesn't mean that's how it will&nbsp;
go down, and with the character confirmed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

